{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Tekhelet.</b> Yefet says it is like the appearance of dawn, for it is the culmination of all colors and all return to it, yet it never reverts in the work of man. We rely on our Rabbis of blessed memory, who said it is green and it is wool." "<b>Argaman.</b> Like red. In Chronicles: ארגון (2 Chronicles 2:6). In Arabic: argawan. This dye occurs only in wool or silk." "<b>Tola'at shani.</b> And it is written ושני התולעת (Leviticus 14:6), like מצור החלמיש (Deuteronomy 8:15) — חלמיש צור (ibid. 32:13). The Gaon [Saadia] rendered it קרימ״ז, for it is red, only it is not like the color of argaman. Because of 'tola'at,' many said it is silk." "<b>Shesh.</b> It is linen, a type among the kinds of flax, found in Egypt alone. It is white and is not dyed. שש ורקמה ממצרים (Ezekiel 27:7). The Gaon [Saadia] translated it in Arabic as 'fine linen,' and it is known to this day." "<b>Izim.</b> Goat hair."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:10.074830279Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}